    "description": "Chapel, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). Needs scaffolding: 13 tall (the bell cote; the nave roof is 9). Over budget: 510 blocks vs 210 (first build 371 vs 170; the L3 churchyard front is 94; 7 wide instead of 5, for two pews a side). Stone chapel (stone bricks on a cobblestone plinth, buttresses, spruce gable roof) whose front gable rises into a bell cote; door under a stone hood, lancet windows, shuttered gable windows, pews, an altar; L2 adds the bell, runner, lectern, candles, lanterns, flower boxes; L3 the churchyard front (a low churchyard wall with a lych gate, old headstones, a stone path, lantern posts), stained glass in the gable windows, banners, candles and flowers.",
    "changes": "Quality check round 1: lanterns on the door hood now stand on flat (upside-down) stair tops; the gable windows are unglazed with open shutters beside them (no inner shutters hiding the L3 stained glass); the back barge board hole is closed; L3 adds a walled churchyard front: a low wall with a lych gate and banners, side walls with lantern piers, old headstones, a stone path to the door and lantern posts (the box grew 4 rows at the front).",
